Z||000017||DRH||01-10-2000||02:48 PM||||Cliff,<P>I'm not real good on Unix and what little I know is on HP. One way to schedule background jobs is the 'at' command. These jobs are run at the appropriate time(s) by the 'cron' process which always runs in the background. Might try looking at documentation on the above commands. Does Linux have 'man' help? <P>David.||||reg||1
